/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Guest material NEVER belongs in this repo. See CLAUDE.md principle 1 and the
# `provenance` job in .github/workflows/ci.yml, which fails the build if any of
# it is committed. These entries are a convenience, not the control.
/dumps/
/firmware/
/games/
*.pkg
*.prx
*.sprx
*.self
eboot.bin
*.pup

# Test corpus (D042). Downloaded homebrew and user-supplied material. Never tracked.
# Named `titles/` rather than `games/` because the provenance guard bans that path.
#
# `/titles/*` rather than `/titles/`: a trailing slash makes git skip the directory
# outright, so the README exception below would never be reachable.
/titles/*
!/titles/README.md

# Local run state (portable-first: everything lands beside the binary)
/.portable/
/traces/

# Pages bundle assembled by `./orbistoun.sh site` (pages.yml builds its own).
/site/


# Scratch. Ad-hoc debug scripts belong on somebody's disk, not in the history - and
# `git add -A` on a repository with no commits stages everything, so the only thing
# standing between a one-off diagnostic and the first commit is this list.
#
# The interpreter-file entries are not leftovers. This repository is Rust and shell; they
# are here so a stray one-off script cannot arrive unnoticed.
/.diag*
/scratch/
*.tmp
# No `__pycache__/` or `*.pyc` rule, deliberately. There is no Python in this repository and
# there is not meant to be - the checks and the build scripts are shell. An ignore rule for
# bytecode is a quiet accommodation for a language that is not allowed here: it would hide the
# first stray file rather than let `git status` show it.

# Outgoing proposals. Generated from measurements and regenerated on demand, so tracking
# them would commit a derived artefact - and a patch worth keeping is a commit, not a file.
/patches/

# The Windows build directory, for the icon-bearing executable.
/target-win/

# Claude Code's per-person overrides. `settings.json` beside it IS shared - SELFish uses it to
# deny reads and edits of `escalation.*` - but the `.local` one is whoever is sitting here, and
# tracking it means their overrides arrive in everybody else's clone. SELFish had it committed
# as a byte-identical copy of the shared file, which is the shape this prevents.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Whatever the person editing this happens to run. None of it is anybody else's business,
# and every one of these has been committed to some repository by accident at least once.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
